---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';

const entry = {
  "id": "harvard_ii3_52",
  "series": "Band II 3 (1695 - 1700)",
  "seq": 52,
  "text": "<p> [[149.1]] <b>52. LEIBNIZ AN VINCENT PLACCIUS</p>\n<p> [[149.2]] Hannover, 27. März (6. April) 1696. [49.56.]</b></p>\n\n<p> [[149.9]] Vir Nobilissime et Consultissime, Fautor Honoratissime </p>\n<p> [[149.10]] Paulo distractior indies responsum distuli, etsi nihil mihi sit gratius quam de rebus\n[[149.11]] profuturis Tecum conferre, cujus sensa meis respondent. </p>\n<p> [[149.12]] De Domino Hinüber ut hoc primum absolvam ita existimo et posse ipsum praestare\n[[149.13]] aliquid, et velle. Amicus Hildesiensis, a quo mihi commendatus fuit, testimonio eum ornavit\n[[149.14]] honorifico, et cum ipse coram non imminuerit conceptam opinionem, putaverim expectationi\n[[149.15]] quoque Tuae responsurum. </p>\n<p> [[149.16]] Cum occasiones mittendi aliquid in Italiam praeterierint, expectanda[e] sunt novae, neque\n[[149.17]] ego negligam significare si quid sese obtulerit. </p>\n<p> [[149.18]] Nunc ad caput rei venio, Cogitationes scilicet de juvanda Republica per profectum solidae\n[[149.19]] doctrinae. Equidem ita sentio, si homines praeclaras veritates ac profuturas intelligerent atque\n[[149.20]] in oculis haberent, haud dubie etiam vitam doctrinae responsuram. Nunc recitant [recte] dogma\n[[149.21]] potius quam capiunt, cum fontes ipsis non sint aperti, et quod non capiunt nec curant. Plerosque\n[[149.22]] video magis Historicis narrationibus quam rerum rationibus delectari, in quibus tamen solis\n[[149.23]] animi perfectio consistit. Interim cogimur accommodare nos humanae imbecillitati, et utilia\n[[149.24]] jucundis condire. Itaque fateor valde profuturam Historiam literariam, sed qu[a]e non tantum\n[[149.25]] historia hominum absolveretur, sed daret progressus quoque cognitionis nostrae. Cogitavi\n[[149.26]] aliquando de Cimeliis nonnullis literariis publicandis. Habeo enim quaedam inedita Galilaei,\n[[149.27]] Cartesii, [Campanellae], Valeriani Magni, Pascalii, quibus fortasse non inutiliter adderentur\n[[150.1]] Jungiana qua[e]dam; nam Jungium nullo illorum inferiorem censeo. His adjungerem animadversiones\n[[150.2]] quasdam in <i>vitam Cartesii</i> a Bailleto editam. Videram dudum compendium ejus,\n[[150.3]] quod fere solum ad has oras pervenit, sed nunc nactus sum ipsum opus majus redemtum ex\n[[150.4]] Bibliotheca Hugeniana in Batavis vendita, cui ipse Hugenius quaedam notatu digna manu sua\n[[150.5]] appinxit. Video Bailletum quaedam in librum suum ex Epistola mea ad Amicum, Bailleti\n[[150.6]] nomine rogantem, Roma scripta, transtulisse; mentione etiam nominis mei facta, sed non ea\n[[150.7]] ingenuitate usum quae conveniebat veritatis magis quam Cartesii amico. Nam ea tantum retulit\n[[150.8]] quae in laudem Cartesii dixeram, suppressis naevis quos notaram. Cogita quaeso, quidnam inter\n[[150.9]] Jungiana breve et selectum addi posse commode putes. </p>\n<p> [[150.10]] Nihil utique utilius est quam eruditos coire in societates. Optandum esset unam esse\n[[150.11]] universalem sed velut in Collegia diversa distinctam tanta enim est inter se connexio diversarum\n[[150.12]] eruditionis partium, ut non magis quam mutuo consensu et conspiratione quadam juvari\n[[150.13]] possint. Sed quando vix est ut sperari nunc tale quiddam possit (: nisi major accedat auctoritas :)\n[[150.14]] contentos nos esse oportet diversis societatibus quas tandem ipsa rerum ratio connectet.\n[[150.15]] Itaque vellem Collegium Historiae patriae illustrandae destinatum urgeri a viris doctis paulo\n[[150.16]] excitatius quam fieri video. Dn. Ludolphus praeses queritur collegas per varia distractos, non\n[[150.17]] satis de collegio cogitare. Suasi ne statim ad elaborationes properarent, sed potius apparatum\n[[150.18]] pro suo quisque modulo conferrent. Multa obtuli de meo, cum faveant his studiis aulae nostrae. </p>\n<p> [[150.19]] Maximam partem eorum quae edidit aut praestitit Dn. Weigelius, vidi vel probo. Ita est, ut\n[[150.20]] scribis, non opus est necessario Magnatibus ad emendationem educationis, sed sufficerent\n[[150.21]] privati conatus, si modo adessent juvenes ingeniosi, docti, pii, laboriosi, addo et externa\n[[150.22]] quadam [specie] atque eloquentia validi, qui si tales scholas aperire vellent, quales optamus,\n[[150.23]] haud dubie mox in se omnium animos converterent. Sed si qui tales sunt malunt plausibiliora\n[[150.24]] agere. Apud pontificios Scholae etiam triviales religionis auctoritate commendantur, apud nos\n[[150.25]] summa injuria ne dicam stultitia, contemtae ac pene sordidae habentur; ut nisi quis singulari\n[[150.26]] quodam zelo et impulsu superiore huc feratur, vix sit in tale ergastulum descensurus. Tales\n[[150.27]] igitur juvenes quaerendi sunt nec desperem posse reperiri, pr[a]esertim in Academiis et in\n[[150.28]] mag[n]is urbibus. Inter infelicia bonorum consiliorum impedimenta etiam pietisticas lites\n[[150.29]] refero, quae faciunt ut innocentissima etiam suspecta habeantur. </p>\n<p> [[151.1]] <i>Scholam virtutum Viennensem</i> habui, nu[n]c habeam nec ne incertum est, [hactenus] enim\n[[151.2]] frustra quaesivi in librorum indigestorum massa. </p>\n<p> [[151.3]] Fuit hic per dies aliquo[t] Franciscus Mercurius Helmontius cum quo mihi fuere quotidiani\n[[151.4]] sermones. Praeclare animatum reperio ad juvandum publicum supra quam facile credas,\n[[151.5]] tametsi paradoxa ejus in iis rebus quibus theologia miscetur seponam. Is in juventutis quoque\n[[151.6]] profectibus augendis et variis artibus atque doctrinis egregia monere potest. Promisit ad nos in\n[[151.7]] reditu revisere. Cum Electrice nostra maximi ingenii Principe multa illi necessitudo ab antiquo,\n[[151.8]] nam ante multos annos apud Electorem ejus fratrem Heidelbergae quotidianus fuerat. Sed et\n[[151.9]] mihi cum eo notitia fuit inde ab anno 1671. Cujus probe meminerat ipse. Toto pene tempore,\n[[151.10]] quo hic fuit, quotidie hora circiter nona matutina in Electricis conclavi convenimus, quo\n[[151.11]] tempore nondum aliis aditus datur, et ipsa praesente de variis rebus sumus collocuti. Solet ille\n[[151.12]] sua per miras ambages dicere, eamque ob rem paucis auditoribus intelligebatur. Mihi vero quo\n[[151.13]] tenderet facile prospicienti jucunda ejus consuetudo fuit. Sed gravis aetas viri facit ut valetudini\n[[151.14]] ejus timeam tam incommodo tempore iter facientis. Nam ab octogenario non multum abest.\n[[151.15]] Sulsbacum ire sese dictitabat ad visendum Principem veterem amicum a quo fuit invitatus.\n[[151.16]] Multa ipsi illic cum Knorrio Rosenrothio familiaritas fuerat Cancellariae [principalis] directore\n[[151.17]] sed jam defuncto viro in omni doctrinae genere ipsisque Judaeorum interioribus egregie\n[[151.18]] versato, quod <i>Cabala denudata</i> ostendit. Cum Sulsbaci transirem monstravit mihi librum a se\n[[151.19]] compositum titulo: <i>Messias puer</i>, in quo Christi nativitas, et pueritia ex Hebreorum doctrina\n[[151.20]] illustrabatur. Sed de his nunc quidem satis. Vale et [me] ama. </p>\n<p> [[151.21]] Dabam Hannoverae 27. Martii 1696. </p>\n",
  "number": "52.",
  "title": "LEIBNIZ AN VINCENT PLACCIUS",
  "date": "Hannover, 27. März (6. April) 1696. [49.56.]"
};
---

<Layout title={`${entry.title || entry.id} - Leibniz Writings`}>
  <article data-pagefind-body>
    <header class="entry-header">
      <h1 data-pagefind-meta="title">{entry.title || entry.id}</h1>

      <div class="entry-meta">
        {entry.date && (
          <div class="meta-item">
            <strong>Date:</strong>
            <span data-pagefind-meta="date">{entry.date}</span>
          </div>
        )}

        <div class="meta-item">
          <strong>Series:</strong>
          <span data-pagefind-meta="series">{entry.series}</span>
        </div>

        {entry.number && (
          <div class="meta-item">
            <strong>Number:</strong>
            <span data-pagefind-meta="number">{entry.number}</span>
          </div>
        )}

        <div class="meta-item">
          <strong>Sequence:</strong>
          <span>{entry.seq}</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </header>

    <!-- View Toggle -->
    <div class="view-controls">
      <button id="translation-view-btn" class="view-btn active">Translation View</button>
      <button id="scholarly-view-btn" class="view-btn">Scholarly View</button>
    </div>

    <div class="entry-content" data-pagefind-meta="excerpt:52. LEIBNIZ AN VINCENT PLACCIUS Hannover, 27. März (6. April) 1696. [49.56.] Vir Nobilissime et Consultissime, Fautor Honoratissime Paulo distractior indies responsum distuli, etsi nihil mihi sit gratius quam de rebus profuturis Tecum conferre, cujus sensa meis respondent. De Domino Hinüber ut hoc p...">

      <!-- Translation-friendly continuous text -->
      <div id="translation-view" class="text-view active">
        <div class="translation-notice">
          <p><strong>📖 Translation View:</strong> Continuous text optimized for browser translation tools.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="continuous-text" translate="yes" lang="unknown" id="continuous-text">
          <!-- Will be populated by JavaScript -->
        </div>
        <div class="line-numbers-reference" id="line-numbers-ref">
          <!-- Will be populated by JavaScript -->
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Detailed scholarly view with line numbers -->
      <div id="scholarly-view" class="text-view">
        <div class="scholarly-notice">
          <p><strong>📚 Scholarly View:</strong> Original text with line number annotations preserved.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="annotated-text" id="annotated-text">
          {entry.text.split('\n').map(paragraph =>
            paragraph.trim() && <p set:html={paragraph} />
          )}
        </div>
      </div>

    </div>
  </article>

  <nav class="entry-navigation">
    <a href="/" class="back-link">← Back to Search</a>
  </nav>
</Layout>

<style>
  .entry-header {
    margin-bottom: 30px;
    padding-bottom: 20px;
    border-bottom: 2px solid var(--border);
  }

  .entry-header h1 {
    color: var(--primary);
    font-size: 2rem;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    line-height: 1.3;
  }

  .entry-meta {
    display: grid;
    gap: 8px;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }

  .meta-item {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    gap: 8px;
  }

  .meta-item strong {
    color: var(--text);
    min-width: 80px;
  }

  .meta-item span {
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    flex: 1;
  }

  .entry-content {
    margin-bottom: 40px;
  }

  .text-content {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 30px;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  .text-content :global(p) {
    margin-bottom: 16px;
  }

  .text-content :global(p:last-child) {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .text-content :global(b) {
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--primary);
  }

  .entry-navigation {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
    padding-top: 20px;
  }

  .back-link {
    color: var(--primary);
    text-decoration: none;
    font-weight: 500;
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 8px;
    transition: color 0.2s;
  }

  .back-link:hover {
    color: var(--primary-dark);
    text-decoration: underline;
  }

  /* View Toggle Controls */
  .view-controls {
    display: flex;
    gap: 8px;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
    padding-bottom: 20px;
  }

  .view-btn {
    background: transparent;
    border: 2px solid var(--border);
    padding: 8px 16px;
    border-radius: 6px;
    cursor: pointer;
    font-size: 14px;
    font-weight: 500;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    transition: all 0.2s;
  }

  .view-btn:hover {
    border-color: var(--primary);
    color: var(--primary);
  }

  .view-btn.active {
    background: var(--primary);
    border-color: var(--primary);
    color: white;
  }

  /* Text Views */
  .text-view {
    display: none;
  }

  .text-view.active {
    display: block;
  }

  /* Translation View */
  .translation-notice, .scholarly-notice {
    background: var(--background);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 6px;
    padding: 12px;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    font-size: 14px;
  }

  .continuous-text {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 2px solid var(--primary);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 25px;
    line-height: 1.8;
    font-size: 16px;
    color: var(--text);
    margin-bottom: 15px;
  }

  .line-numbers-reference {
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    font-size: 13px;
    padding: 10px;
    background: var(--background);
    border-radius: 4px;
  }

  /* Scholarly View */
  .annotated-text {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 20px;
  }

  .text-line {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    margin-bottom: 8px;
    gap: 12px;
  }

  .line-refs {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 4px;
    min-width: 80px;
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }

  .line-num {
    background: var(--primary);
    color: white;
    padding: 2px 6px;
    border-radius: 4px;
    font-size: 11px;
    font-weight: 600;
    font-family: monospace;
  }

  .line-content {
    flex: 1;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .line-content :global(b) {
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--primary);
  }

  .line-content :global(i) {
    font-style: italic;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
  }

  @media (min-width: 768px) {
    .entry-meta {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    .view-controls {
      flex-direction: column;
    }

    .text-line {
      flex-direction: column;
      gap: 6px;
    }

    .line-refs {
      min-width: auto;
    }
  }
</style>

<script>
  // Process text for translation view
  function processTextForTranslation(text) {
    if (!text) return { translationText: '', lineNumbers: [] };

    const lines = text.split('\n');
    let translationText = '';
    const lineNumbers = [];

    lines.forEach(line => {
      const trimmedLine = line.trim();
      if (!trimmedLine) return;

      // Extract line numbers
      const lineNumberMatch = trimmedLine.match(/\[\[(\d+\.\d+)\]\]/g);
      const extractedNumbers = lineNumberMatch ?
        lineNumberMatch.map(m => m.replace(/\[|\]/g, '')) : [];

      // Remove line number markers and HTML tags for continuous text
      let contentOnly = trimmedLine
        .replace(/\[\[\d+\.\d+\]\]/g, '')
        .replace(/<\/?[^>]+(>|$)/g, '')
        .replace(/\s+/g, ' ')
        .trim();

      if (contentOnly) {
        if (translationText) translationText += ' ';
        translationText += contentOnly;
        lineNumbers.push(...extractedNumbers);
      }
    });

    return {
      translationText: translationText.trim(),
      lineNumbers: lineNumbers
    };
  }

  // View switching and text processing
  document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', () => {
    const translationBtn = document.getElementById('translation-view-btn');
    const scholarlyBtn = document.getElementById('scholarly-view-btn');
    const translationView = document.getElementById('translation-view');
    const scholarlyView = document.getElementById('scholarly-view');
    const continuousTextDiv = document.getElementById('continuous-text');
    const lineNumbersRef = document.getElementById('line-numbers-ref');

    // Process the text for translation view
    if (continuousTextDiv && lineNumbersRef && entry && entry.text) {
      const processed = processTextForTranslation(entry.text);
      continuousTextDiv.textContent = processed.translationText;

      if (processed.lineNumbers.length > 0) {
        lineNumbersRef.innerHTML = `<small><strong>Line numbers:</strong> ${processed.lineNumbers.join(', ')}</small>`;
      }
    }

    // View switching functionality
    if (translationBtn && scholarlyBtn && translationView && scholarlyView) {
      translationBtn.addEventListener('click', () => {
        translationBtn.classList.add('active');
        scholarlyBtn.classList.remove('active');
        translationView.classList.add('active');
        scholarlyView.classList.remove('active');
      });

      scholarlyBtn.addEventListener('click', () => {
        scholarlyBtn.classList.add('active');
        translationBtn.classList.remove('active');
        scholarlyView.classList.add('active');
        translationView.classList.remove('active');
      });
    }
  });
</script>